Sean,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on lodges, re=
serves and farms; we don't sell packages.

Fort Governor's runs three off-grid lodges and walk-and-stalk hunting across =
more than 10,000 ha. On a hunting estate communications are a safety matter f=
irst: parties spread across the property, staff at three lodges, and the need=
 to reach someone fast if something goes wrong in the field.

We've done a desktop terrain study of the estate from 30 m satellite elevatio=
n data and cloud-free imagery. It's attached, one page, no pricing. What it f=
ound:

- The estate has real height to work with: a southern high site at about 850 =
m and a northern one at about 540 m, 9.7 km apart with a clear path between t=
hem.
- All three lodges are on clear paths: Mountain Retreat 1.0 km from the north=
ern site, Uniondale 2.4 km and Stoneyvale 7.1 km from the southern site. Unio=
ndale is the tightest of the three and the one to confirm first.
- A candidate carrier uplink of 16.4 km from the Makhanda high ground into th=
e southern site, with generous clearance.
- About 60% of the 77 km2 study area is in line of sight of the two sites, wh=
ich is where the hunting areas, gates and vehicles would be reached.

Those positions are desktop candidates until we walk them. What the study say=
s is that one small owned backbone, two masts and one uplink, can carry all t=
hree lodges and most of the ground between them.

The next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you have, what fails, wh=
at it costs you, and what an owned network would look like, with the high sit=
es confirmed on the ground. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against the build, and th=
e report is yours either way. If you share the lodges' current connectivity i=
nvoices, I'll put the estate's actual payback in that report.

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

